vk_scheduler: switch to pause, not reset, the occlusion counter at each submission

Ported from zortos293/Lichii #121, still open there, both commits by Kajcsi:
e3cf9394c1 (pause) and 47e1e95208 (bound the running query).
EndPendingOperations ran CounterReset before every submission. A submission
landing between a guest's counter reset and its report dropped the samples
counted so far, so the report read too low, often 0, and Ocarina took it as
occluded for one frame: Link went white. The split GPU thread and its deferred
fence flushes make that frequent, and both are on by default here.

A paused query runs on until the guest resets or reports it. Ocarina does
neither on its title screen and file select, and it reached 16,384 slots over 64
sample banks. The second commit drops the count, as a reset would, once a query
passes one bank (256 slots). The longest gameplay window measured was 36 slots.

EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_PAUSE=1 turns all of this on. Default off, which keeps the old
reset; only this path reaches the samples CloseCounter. The switch is ours, the
source has none. Inc0rporate reports on that PR that an RX 9070 XT with the
split on, GPU accuracy Low, hangs in Ocarina right after picking the save with
the first commit (WaitSubmitted never ends), and PS5 is AMD with the split on
too. The same build with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=0 neither hung nor flashed. The source
author thinks the second commit fixes it but could not reproduce the hang on
NVIDIA, and it has not been retested on AMD. The source also reports one rarer
flash left afterwards, not yet explained.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
index f63c924..c2d9bc9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
@@ -209,8 +209,17 @@ public:
         last_accumulation_checkpoint = (std::max)(last_accumulation_checkpoint, num_slots_used);
     }
 
+    // Called at each submission with EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_PAUSE=1. The running query carries the count
+    // across it: a guest's reset-to-report window can span one.
     void CloseCounter() override {
         PauseCounter();
+        // A title that counts without resetting or reporting grows the query by a slot at every
+        // submission and render pass, and the query keeps every bank it touches alive. Ocarina of
+        // Time's title screen and file select reached 16,384 slots over 64 banks (its gameplay
+        // windows span at most 36 slots). Past a bank, drop the count as a reset would.
+        if (current_query && current_query->size_slots > SamplesQueryBank::BANK_SIZE) {
+            ResetCounter();
+        }
     }
 
     bool HasPendingSync() const override {
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
index f23e07e..ce1851d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp
@@ -474,7 +474,20 @@ void Scheduler::InvalidateState() {
 }
 
 void Scheduler::EndPendingOperations() {
-    query_cache->CounterReset(VideoCommon::QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64);
+    // EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_PAUSE=1: pause, don't reset. A submission can land between a guest's counter
+    // reset and its report, and resetting here drops the samples counted so far (the report then
+    // reads too low). Off by default: with the split on, pausing hung an AMD host at a game's save
+    // select (Lichii #121), and the bound in SamplesStreamer::CloseCounter meant to stop that has
+    // not been tried on AMD yet.
+    static const bool pause_zpass = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_ZPASS_PAUSE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (pause_zpass) {
+        query_cache->CounterClose(VideoCommon::QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64);
+    } else {
+        query_cache->CounterReset(VideoCommon::QueryType::ZPassPixelCount64);
+    }
     EndRenderPass();
 }
 
